{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"gothic rock\" \"genre\" (+ themes lyrics characteristics) (+ death melancholy existentialism nihilism romanticism morbidity))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1235371375#2_1362283104","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2366","rank":6,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1235371375#2_1362283104\" , \"end_char\": 2989.000000 , \"headings\": \"Goth subculture Goth subculture Contents Music Origins and development Gothic <cover>genre Art, historical and cultural influences 18th and 19th centuries Visual art influences 20th century influences 21st century Characteristics of the scene Icons Fashion Influences Styling Reciprocity Critique Films Books and magazines Graphic art Events Interior design Sociology Gender and sexuality Identity Media and academic commentary Perception on nonviolence School shootings Prejudice and violence directed at goths Self-harm study See also References Citations Bibliography Further reading \" , \"segment\": \"The subculture has associated tastes in music, aesthetics, and fashion. The music preferred by goths includes a number of styles such as gothic rock, death </cover>rock, post-punk, cold wave, dark wave, and ethereal wave. Styles of dress within the subculture draw on punk, new wave, and New Romantic fashion. It also draws from the fashion of earlier periods such as the Victorian, Edwardian, and Belle Époque eras. The style most often includes dark (usually solid black) attire, dark makeup, and black hair. The subculture ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1236837256#1_1363400322","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1236837256#0_1363397743","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_237360052#8_262516369","rank":3,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1236837256#2_1363402518","rank":4,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_237360052#7_262514012","rank":5,"relevance":1}]}}
