{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1236764777#8_1363374949","relevance":1,"reason":"The result is about gothic metal, not goth/gothic rock. It provides adjacent evidence about gothic-metal themes such as death, misery, lost love, romance, and personal experience, but it does not directly answer what issues goth rock addressed.","learned":"Gothic metal sources continue to dominate some theme queries and are only indirect evidence for goth rock."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"gothic rock\" (+ \"personal themes\" \"social themes\" alienation depression suicide self-harm) (+ lyrics subculture))","reason":"Search for direct discussions of gothic rock lyrics or its subculture around social-emotional issues such as alienation, depression, suicide, and self-harm, which may better match the user's 'society issues' wording."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"gothic rock\" (+ \"personal themes\" \"social themes\" alienation depression suicide self-harm) (+ lyrics subculture))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1236764777#7_1363372733","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2378","rank":2,"snippet":"Sonic traits Vocals Lyrics History Precursors Heavy metal Gothic rock Origins The Peaceville Three Other pioneers Development Beauty and the beast Symphonic gothic metal Commercial success Paradise Lost Cradle of Filth Moonspell and Within Temptation Lacuna Coil Evanescence HIM Finnish scene See also Notes References External links \" , \"segment\": \"For the three English bands that helped to pioneer the genre, their gloomy lyrics reflect their background in doom metal while their darker or melodramatic lyrics draw influence from <cover>gothic rock. The music of My Dying Bride has been noted as \"dripping with treachery and pain\" from a \"lyrical fascination with deceit and transgressions of every variety\". Lyrics that focus on suicide </cover>and the meaninglessness of life can be found in Anathema while Paradise Lost too has \"never lost their depressive edge\". The Italian gothic black metal band Theatres des Vampires manifests a deep interest in the vampire myth, a common staple of gothic horror fiction. Gothic fiction, a literary genre that blends horror and romance, has been a source of inspiration for the lyrics of many gothic metal bands like Cadaveria, Cradle of Filth, Moonspell, Theatres des Vampires and Xandria. Critic Eduardo Rivadavia of Allmusic ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1236764777#6_1363370445","rank":1,"relevance":1}]}}
